ENTRY            G0108   20251126   20261124   20261124       G061
SUBENT        G0108001   20251126   20261124   20261124       G061
BIB                 12         43
TITLE      A substitution measurement for cross section of
            65Cu(g,n)64Cu reaction using natCu and 63Cu targets
            by quasi-monoenergetic beams at SLEGS
AUTHOR     (Pu Jiao, Zi-Rui Hao, Zhi-Cai Li, Qian-Kun Sun,
            Long-Xiang Liu, Hang-Hua Xu, Yue Zhang, Meng-Die Zhou,
            Wen Luo, Yu-Xuan Yang, Sheng Jin, Kai-Jie Chen,
            Shan Ye, Zhen-Wei Wang, Yu-Ting Wang, Hui-Ling Wei,
            Yao Fu, Kun Yu, Hong-Wei Wang, Gong-Tao Fan,
            Chun-Wang Ma)
REFERENCE  (J,CNST,36,240,2025)
INSTITUTE  (3CPRARI,3CPRNRS,3CPRUCA,3CPRAEP)
           (3CPRCPR) Henan Normal Univ., Xinxiang; Univ. of South
            China, Hengyang; Zhengzhou University, Zhengzhou;
            ShanghaiTech University, Shanghai; Institute of
            Nuclear Science and Technology, Henan Academy of
            Sciences, Zhengzhou
FACILITY   (ESTRG,3CPRARI) 3.5 GeV storage ring of Shanghai Laser
            Electron Gamma Source (SLEGS)
INC-SOURCE (LCS) 100W CO2 laser photons (wavelength 10.64 um)
            scattered by 3.5 GeV electrons
SAMPLE     Natural Cu (3.15 g, 10.00 mm in diameter x 4.48 mm
            thick, 8.69 g/cm3, chemical purity higher than 99.99%)
            in polyethylene target holders.
           (29-CU-63,NAT=0.6915)
           (29-CU-65,NAT=0.3085)
DETECTOR   (HE3SP) 3He flat efficiency detector (FED) with
            26 proportional counters in three concentric radii
            within a polyethylene moderator shielded by a 2 mm Cd
            sheet
           (BGO) for gamma flux measurement
METHOD     (RINGR) for neutron detection efficiency determination
ANALYSIS   (UNFLD) unfolding with LCS photon energy profile
            measured by the BGO detector
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S) statistical uncertainty
           (ERR-1) systematic uncertainty due to
                   . gamma flux caused by Cu attenuator  (0.50%)
                   . target thickness                   (<0.10%)
                   . neutron detector efficiency         (3.02%)
           (ERR-2) methodological uncertainty due to
                   . determination of number of neutrons (2.00%)
                   . BGO response matrix simulation      (1.00%)
           (ERR-T) total uncertainty
HISTORY    (20251126C) On
ENDBIB              43
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           46
SUBENT        G0108002   20251126   20261124   20261124       G061
BIB                  4          6
REACTION   (29-CU-65(G,N)29-CU-64,,SIG,,,DERIV)
ANALYSIS   63Cu(g,n)62Cu contribution subtracted by adopting its
            cross sections measured at SLEGS
REL-REF    (R,G0093002,Zhi-Cai Li+,J,CNST,36,34,2025)
            63Cu(g,n)62Cu cross sections measured at SLEGS
STATUS     (TABLE,,Pu Jiao+,J,CNST,36,240,2025) Table 3
ENDBIB               6
